{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Welcome to UML \"Unified Modelling Language\""}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about UML. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Explain important features related to object programming in different contexts and with different types of object programming"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Present Tense Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <strong> the simple present tense</strong> to talk about routines and daily activities."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Does UML play an important role in software programming?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Does UML have any kind of established procedures?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It's time to review the simple present tense in all its forms (affirmative, negative, and questions)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Affirmative:</strong> When we use present simple in affirmative sentences, we just need to be careful when conjugating the verbs since the verbs are different for the subjects in third person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\"center\"><ul><ul> Subject + <strong>verb</strong> + complement"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>I <strong>use</strong> the unified modeling language to design what I need."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>He <strong>uses</strong> the unified modeling language to design what I need."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Negative:</strong> To present negative statements in simple present, we just need to use the auxiliary do not (don't) and does not (doesn't) depending on the subjects of the sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\"center\"><ul><ul>Subject + <strong>do not (don't) / does (doesn't) </strong>+ verb in base form + complement"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>A Programmer <strong>doesn't</strong> code the software without a previous design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>Programmers <strong>don't</strong> code the software without a previous design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Questions:</strong> To ask questions using present simple you just need to add the auxiliary do or does (depending on the subject of the sentence) at the beginning of the statement. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br> <div align=\"center\"><strong>Do/Does</strong> + subject + verb in base form + complement?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><strong>Do</strong> programmers need a modeling language?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><strong>Does</strong> a programmer need a modeling language?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You need to start your presentation by explaining what UML is. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "UML uses an object-oriented style in software projects."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't understand the concept very well. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Order of Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, there is a specific <strong>order for adjectives</strong> when you need to mention more than one for an object. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The unified modeling language, also known as UML, is a useful and standard language."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I saw some big, rectangular, colorless charts on one of my books."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is the order in which adjectives should appear in case that you need to provide a complete description of something."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Order\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Description\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Opinion\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A useful software\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A big tool\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Physical quality\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A rough description\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Shape\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A square system\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Age\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An old procedure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"6\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A red light\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"7\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Origin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A German software\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"8\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Material\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A plastic device\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"9\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Purpose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A programming device\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Let's see some examples of nouns with more than one adjective:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>I need a <strong>practical, light</strong>, and <strong>new</strong> software for the company.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "model "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a representation of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This model describes software like the different functions of a system from the user's perspective, the systems' attributes, relationships, and objects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "activity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "processes and data flow that occur in a transaction "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Activity which shows the data flow and processes in business transactions. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "class "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "command that shows the type and relationship of components "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are others like Class where you can see the types of data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "component "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "important part of a system "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Component where the major parts of the system appear."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deploy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize objects strategically"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Deployment which is the one that deploys the systems including hardware and software servers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "package "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "elements organized into a group "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Packages where you organize all the elements of the object."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le01ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about more examples of UML diagrams. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what those diagrams are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify their main characteristics. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Provide examples of a situation in which you would implement a diagram."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your findings with a partner. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about UML diagrams. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the features of UML diagrams. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my finding with a partner. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Erik</strong>: Hey Tara, I need your help. I need to prepare a presentation about the unified modeling language for my programming class and I know you are an expert. Do you have time to help me out?</br>\n<strong>Tara</strong>: Definitely! That's one of my favorite topics. You need to start your presentation by explaining what UML is. </br>\n<strong>Erik</strong>: Right. But, I don't understand the concept very well. </br>\n<strong>Tara</strong>: It's very easy. You can start by saying that the unified modeling language, also known as UML, is a useful and standard language that programmers use to design and document a system. UML uses an object-oriented style in software projects."}, {"time": "45000", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Erik</strong>: OK. Does UML play an important role in software programming? </br>\n<strong>Tara</strong>: Of course. This model describes software like the different functions of a system from the user's perspective, the systems' attributes, relationships, and objects. It's important to mention that UML doesn't need the software's coding because it is not necessary to show the design of a software architecture."}, {"time": "73800", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Erik</strong>: Great! So, does UML have any kind of established procedures? I saw some big, rectangular, colorless charts on one of my books.</br>\n<strong>Tara</strong>: Well, there are some diagrams that people use in UML. For example, Activity which shows the data flow and processes in business transactions. There are others like Class where you can see the types of data; Communication where classes exchange messages; Packages where you organize all the elements of the object; Component where the major parts of the system appear. Oh! I almost forgot. Deployment which is the one that deploys the systems including hardware and software servers.</br>\n<strong>Erik</strong>: Thanks a lot, Tara! You are very smart."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le01ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what UML is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand why UML plays an important role in software programming."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give examples of some of diagrams used in UML."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important to design programs before coding them?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the benefits of using a modeling language when designing a software?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "A Standard Language for Designing"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content":